oked into the way  that other people have dealt with this  both in the genre and outside the genre  some of those things we've we've thought  about we've explored right now we're  going for a couple of different takes  weiming the biggest thing for us is just  the game design itself we feel lends  itself towards a different play  experience but we'll also explore some  of those make game features that would  try to combat some of the more  our community elements of the game that  where people who are toxic might cause  you know other players to not have as  much fun yeah for the lever system for  instance you started to talk a little  bit about that I know you haven't really  given too many details and sounds like  that's still being in developed but when  you look at that do you do you see any  issue where maybe like if you encourage  people to to stay in the game long  enough for her to you discourage leavers  enough that there's not that many that  like the queues for these games are  going to get really long for them it  might discourage them from continuing to  play the game do you mean if levers then  have no other levers to get yeah exactly  right it could extend the queue times  right so just to explain a little bit  about what that system is basically  we're talking about if you leave a game  we will match you up with other levers  to play together on your team it doesn't  actually mean that will match you up  against other levers for the opposing  team ok so you don't technically need a  full ten players it might just be fill  out the rest of your team with other  levers at the end of the day though if  we if it truly was such a small number  that they had a hard time getting of the  games i actually think we've won okay  and those few players that couldn't make  it into a game unfortunately they're the  outliers yeah so does that mean that  maybe the the team that goes up against  a team that doesn't have a bunch of  levers on it they're like we got the  leaver team guys it's going to be an  easy way I'm not sure that we're gonna  like call that out to AO that it's a  leader team but when you start to see  two or three guys leave you're like oh  it's one of those if they continue along  with that style of play then yeah you'll  know when people are just leaving a game  either that either you think you're  doing awesome or there are a team of  leaders yeah now whenever I talk to  Chris last year there's a little bit  discussion around a competitive eSports  stuff and obviously you guys are a  company that has a heritage of these  eSports titles at the time you said well  you know we're still kind of figuring  out how the community will approach the  game and if they're interested in it but  here you guys are holding a tournament  lots of notable past eSports players  participating where are you guys at in  terms of you know feeling about the game  in terms of an eSports title or maybe a  competitive title sure at the end of the  day like we're going to support this  game in however the community wants so I  think that's what Chris was speaking to  previously when you talk to him is that  if a lot of our games from an eSports  perspective they've developed or gay  the community has shown us that hey we  really want this to be any sport so for  Heroes it's kind of the same thing where  we're waiting to kind of see a little  bit how this works out but at the same  time we've already started seeing that  even though we're in technical alpha the  game's not done we don't even have  everyone playing the game yet we already  see teams forming around it tournaments  starting to you know be played and so  we're trying to embrace that and support  that as much as possible the invitation  on the exhibition games we have here are  kind of an example of that we added  custom games back in we added the  initial observer mode to kind of support  this so that we can kind of see where  this goes at the same time we're also  discussing internally what we're going  to do for east boards for heroes of the  storm and we're definitely going to  support it ok very good so yeah as you  see this stuff happen as you create the  Invitational here and you have this how  does that inform you know where you you  put resources maybe four features or  that kind of thing yeah i mean the  esports guys and girls are always  talking to us about hey we could really  use this or that i mean some of our  motivations of putting the initial  observer mode and custom games back in  the game was purely because esports was  saying look people are chomping at the  bit right now they want to get get this  in as a tournament and so we threw it  back in so we're just like in starcraft  we embrace these words we love you  sports and a lot of features we put into  starcraft we're solely just for eSports  we're probably going to do the same  thing with heroes and support it in any  way we can in terms of the free-to-play  sort of like market features and in-game  cus purchasable items and different  things you guys doing with skins and all  that how do you feel about the current  model that you guys have is it is it are  you guys pretty comfortable with as that  something that we should see or expect  to see continued into closed beta and  beyond yeah i think i think the model is  working for us we're still exploring it  it's still early so this is a technical  alpha we haven't invited everyone in yet  but for the most part we're actually  very happy with the direction it's going  we feel that there's an easy way for you  to jump in and play a good amount of  this game we've got the hero rotation  depending on what level you get to  you'll be able to unlock basically play  for free seven heroes every week so  there's a there's a good amount of game  that you can get without actually paying  any money to us at all and then over  time as you learn the game and you want  to kind of keep playing some of those  heroes you can purchase them purchase  skins things like that so this is kind  of a maybe broader question about the  company but I'm really happy to ask you  this question because it kind of ties  into heroes of the storm you guys have  now just announced a new game at  blizzard ever you know I used to play  wow way back Warcraft etc during that  time you guys have gone from a company  that you know has maybe one title that  you've announced for development to now  you have all these different things many  games that are continuing to be  developed even after launch what is it  like because heroes is kind of you know  not to make the pun but the Nexus of  this idea of all these different titles  and games and that kind of thing what is  it like to be working on this project  that is tied into all the stuff that's  continuing to grow I mean we just saw  overwatch today yeah it's it's awesome  and I know if you talk to the artist  they'll tell you it's even more awesome  because they get to actually touch all  the different universes they get to  bring in those the the characters the  heroes the villains that you're so used  to from all the different games and  bring them all into one space and so  there's a lot of creative stuff we can  do we have a lot of liberties because of  this whole nexus concept and you know  we're not taking the lower so specific  and so seriously that you can't have  Arthas fighting rain or things like that  so as we make more games it just means  more things to pull from that's why we  literally have this kind of unending  source of heroes and battlegrounds that  we can choose from sorry tying into that  you guys announced I think three  Warcraft universe heroes today also lost  vikings what determines are you know  what what decides were you're pulling  from or what kind of heroes from sharon  lee all the different options it gets  head so there's a lot of things that go  into that um some of it is what we  currently need in the game if maybe we  need another support or we need another  assassin we might lean heavily on that  side the other one is what fans ask for  like for example lost vikings last year  when we were at blizzcon we had a lot of  feedback hey what about lost vikings  what about some of these older games  that you guys used to make and literally  a year later here we are there in the  game so there's a lot of different  things that go into it we also want to  keep a nice representation across the  universe  so if we're getting a little bit to  warcraft heavy we might you know bring  in some more Diablo and starcraft things  like that I just imagine at the blizzard  offices you guys must have like a giant  whiteboard with a bunch of names  scribbled on it from all this different  stuff yep along those lines you guys  just announced overwatch actually feel  like I think the background of the  presentation today had one of the new  heroes from overwatch and it uh what  should we expect from overwatch in terms  of heroes of the storm so we don't have  anything to announce yet but just like  you know the fact that we just got done  talking about how we can pull these  heroes from our other games I would not  be surprised to see overwatch characters  and heroes at some point in the future  very good I actually that about wraps up  all of my questions but I just want to  thank you so much for the interview  anything that players should expect to  see or any big differences as we head  into the closed beta I think you're just  going to see more content more heroes  more battlegrounds more features we  talked about ranked play we talked about  the draft mode coming up we're going to  keep inviting more players we're really  excited to have everyone in this game I  know there's a lot of people who want to  get in it's just growing and growing in  this you can kind of feel the energy  behind him well thank you so much for  the interview thank you everyone else  you can check out the rest of our  coverage of all things blizzcon at  gamespot com  you

